WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.946 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Review one detected pattern

00:00:01.946 --> 00:00:03.712 line:92% position:50% size:90%
in its chart context.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.197 line:92% position:50% size:90%
First, check the market

00:00:07.197 --> 00:00:09.214 line:92% position:50% size:90%
and the selected timeframe.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.319 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Open Scanner beneath the chart.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.656 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Choose one result and

00:00:18.656 --> 00:00:20.132 line:92% position:50% size:90%
read the pattern name.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.631 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Check whether its direction is

00:00:25.631 --> 00:00:27.592 line:92% position:50% size:90%
bullish, bearish, or neutral.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.155 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Its score is a review

00:00:31.155 --> 00:00:33.130 line:92% position:50% size:90%
cue, not a win probability.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.199 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Turn on Patterns to see

00:00:37.199 --> 00:00:38.814 line:92% position:50% size:90%
the available chart overlay.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.830 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Compare the overlay with the

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.150 line:92% position:50% size:90%
candles you are viewing.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.981 line:92% position:50% size:90%
Look for evidence that

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:50.783 line:92% position:50% size:90%
could contradict the idea.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.490 line:92% position:50% size:90%
If the setup is unclear,

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.800 line:92% position:50% size:90%
wait and ask your instructor.
